hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27586","Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, he said: Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Busr ibn Said, from Zaynab, wife of Abdullah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: When one of you attends Isha, let her not touch perfume."
"27587","He said: Yaqub and Sad narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Hisham, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Said, he said: Zaynab al-Thaqafiyyah, wife of Abdullah ibn Masud, informed me that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to her: When one of you goes out to Isha, let her not touch perfume."
"27588","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Shaqiq, from Amr ibn al-Harith ibn al-Mustaliq, from the nephew of Zaynab, wife of Abdullah, from Zaynab, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed us and said: O assembly of women, give charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the most of the people of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. She said: Abdullah was a man of little means. I said to him: Ask for me the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether spending upon my husband and orphans in my care suffices me as charity. She said: Awe had been cast upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. He said: Go yourself and ask him. She said: I went and reached his door, and there at it was a woman of the Ansar named Zaynab, her need my need. She said: Bilal came out to us. She said: We said to him: Ask for us the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, whether spending upon our husbands and orphans in our care suffices us as charity. She said: Bilal entered upon him and said: At the door is Zaynab. He said: Which of the Zaynabs? He said: Zaynab, wife of Abdullah, and Zaynab, a woman of the Ansar, asking you about spending upon their husbands and orphans in their care, whether that suffices them as charity. She said: He came out to us and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: For them are two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity."
"27589","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, from Zaynab, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, bequeathed to women their dwellings."
"27590","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Jami ibn Shaddad, from Kulthum, she said: Zaynab used to delouse the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while with him was the wife of Uthman ibn Mazun and women of the emigrants complaining of their dwellings, that they are expelled from them and constrained therein. Zaynab spoke and left the head of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You do not speak with your eyes; speak and do your work. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded that day that the women of the emigrants be bequeathed dwellings. Abdullah died and his wife inherited a house in Madinah."
